<p><FONT face="verdana, tahoma" size="2" >I was born in Florida. I'm a navy brat. Moved about every two years of my young life. CA, MA, MD, VA (3 places).<br>
<br>
My father was raised by an alcoholic twit and a male chauvenist pig. My father was a career Navy man. Was E-9 at the time of his death. He was 6 months from retirement after 22 years in the Navy. Don't know what rank that is, but that's what my ID card used to say. <br>
<br>
My mom was raised by a twit and an asshole. She did go to college and got a degree in education because that's what the asshole wanted. Her real interest was in art. She returned to college in 1998 and got her masters in painting. She met Jamie (circa 1986) and they are still together today, though not legally married. You all can rant about her abusing the government. But she is staying unmarried and has been pulling my father's retirement from the Navy. She will lose it if she marries. My dad earned that money. Besides, the government screwed her. Because dad died 6 months before official retirement, she gets 3/4 the amount. Jamie is a wonderful caring man. I don't consider him my father, but I love him. They didn't have any more kids.<br>
<br>
I have one brother. 2 1/2 years younger than me. I was the hero child. My brother was the scapegoat. If you took any Psych classes, you'll know what I am talking about. I hated my brother. he was mean to me, stole from me for money for drugs etc. 2 months in rehab when he was 17 straightened him out. I think he drinks too much. He went to the National Disel Auto Academy in Nashville. He works on vehicles now.<br>
<br>
My dad was an alcoholic. I used to love the fact that he was out to sea so much. Because when he was home, I did nothing but hid. He had a temper like a volcano. You never knew if he was going to hug you or throw you across the room. He trashed our house repeatdly and got picked up by the MP's several times. I learned to lay low and not trust anyone.  My mom, being used to abuse by the asshole, never questioned what was going on nor protected her children. My dad joined AA in 1982 and was sober about 15 months when he was (ironically) killed by a drunk driver. (I was 14).I don't know if he would have stayed sober, but it PISSSES ME OFF that I never got the chance to find out. He pulled me aside about a month before his death and apologized for being a horrible father. I'm glad he did that. Mom had many years of therapy. I've forgiven her for not being there for me when I was a child. She is a different person now. Actually I've had a little therapy myself.<br>
<br>
I decided this pattern of abuse would not be repeated and ended dates if the guy even drank more than 1 beer. I avoided anyone in the military, because I did not want to move around. I met my husband in college. he was an Army brat and for many of the same reasons, would never enlist in the military. I thank whatever fate, power, god brought us together.<br>
<br>
